  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "A similarity transformation is any transformation made up of rigid motions (rotations, reflections, and translations) and dilations.\n\nA similarity transformation will map any polygon to a similar polygon.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the transformations in turn.\n\n- Transformation I includes stretching with different factors in the $x$- and $y$-direction. Thus, it is not a similarity transformation.\n\n- Transformation II is a combination of two translations, which are rigid motions. Thus, it is a similarity transformation.\n\n- Transformation III is a combination of dilation of scale factor $2$ and a reflection. Thus, it is a similarity transformation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
